{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet","generatedAt":"2026-07-20T04:58:34.963Z","term":"odyssey becomes christopher nolan biggest global debut million","beat":"culture","queryTerms":["odyssey","becomes","christopher","nolan","biggest","global","debut","million"],"sourceCount":7,"selectedCount":5,"intakeSources":[{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.source","subject":"public-web:4a3c23d9f60612c3103fd53cac60f534cdbbf6e500e3d127f6d61bbc031815b1","wire":"culture","path":"urn:public-web-source:44f4aa4d921a7348b3f25d5bc6f897795eaf4a4738854e12ea13a505c3587b67","title":"'The Odyssey' storms box office with a USD 264.1 million global debut; dethrones 'The Dark Knight Rises' as Christopher Nolan's highest film opening","url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/english/hollywood/box-office/the-odyssey-storms-box-office-with-a-usd-264-1-million-global-debut-dethrones-the-dark-knight-rises-as-christopher-nolans-highest-film-opening/articleshow/132501487.cms","domain":"timesofindia.indiatimes.com","published":"2026-07-19T22:49:00.000Z","assertedAt":"2026-07-19T22:49:00.000Z","score":80,"primary":false,"matchedTerms":["odyssey","becomes","christopher","nolan","biggest","global","debut","million"],"summary":"Christopher Nolan's 'The Odyssey' stormed the North American box office to score one of the biggest debuts and a personal record for the director.According to trade reports, the film earned an estimated USD 124.5 million in domestic ticket sales and another USD 139.6 million from overseas, notching an even better debut than 'Oppenheimer' and marking Nolan's best opening since 2012's 'The Dark Knight Rises', which earned USD 249 million at the time of its release.Nolan flexed his singular box-office might with a global debut unlike any other. Few filmmakers alive could pull off a starry, big-budget adaptation of Homer's epic poem. But in a Hollywood where intellectual property rights rule most hits, Nolan turned one of the world's oldest works of literature into an unlikely summer blockbuster.'The Odyssey' becomes most expensive R-rated filmThe Universal production was no small gamble on Nolan, coming off the 2023 best picture-winning 'Oppenheimer'. With a production budget of USD 250 million, it's among the most expensive R-rated movies ever made. Universal is spending some USD 125 million to market it.IMAX drives 'The Odyssey' ticket salesBut no behind-the-camera name turns out audiences more than Nolan's. So great was the hype on 'The Odyssey' that IMAX put tickets on sale for some 70 mm showtimes a full year in advance. To satisfy the extraordinary demand for Nolan's preferred format, IMAX 70 mm, some theaters added midnight and 3 a.m. screenings - and sold them out.Billed as Nolan's first feature shot entirely with IMAX cameras, the format drove a huge slice of ticket sales. That included USD 29.6 million domestically on IMAX and USD 51.8 million globally, leading to the company's best weekend ever.IMAX is dedicating its screens entirely to 'The Odyssey' for three weeks. Though only 41 IMAX screens can screen 'The Odyssey' in 70 mm, they accounted for USD 6.3 million in ticket sales.Since the pandemic, Nolan has been at the forefront of reviving cinemas. His 'Tenet' was one of the first big releases to wade back into theaters in 2020. Three years later, 'Oppenheimer' and Greta Gerwig's 'Barbie' combined to create arguably the movies' signature moment of the decade. 'Oppenheimer' ultimately grossed USD 975 million worldwide.'The Odyssey' arrived in theaters during Hollywood's best summer since 2019. Ticket sales are running 10.4% ahead of last year, according to Rentrak. The industry is expecting the first $10 billion year at the domestic box office since the pandemic.'Spider-Man' to crash 'The Odyssey' partyThe only question for \"The Odyssey\" will be how front-loaded it is, given that many moviegoers have had this weekend circled for months. The film faced no new-release competition over the weekend, and it won't next weekend, either. However, come month-end, the film will face new competition with the release of Tom Holland and Zendaya's 'Spider-Man: Brand New Day' on July 31 (India July 30). The superhero film is touted to make a splash at the box office, and continue its epic box office run, crossing the USD 1 billion mark again.Casting controversy has no apparent effect'The Odyssey' stars Matt Damon as Odysseus and features Holland as his son, Telemachus; Anne Hathaway as Penelope; Zendaya as Athena; Robert Pattinson as the suitor Antinous and Charlize Theron as the sea nymph Calypso.Nolan's casting for the film including Lupita Nyong'o as Helen and Elliot Page as a soldier, was controversial to some conservative commentators. Elon Musk called Nolan a \"coward\" over Nyong'o's casting.But that criticism had little to no effect on 'The Odyssey' becoming one of the big-screen cultural events of the year. Reviews (95% fresh on Rotten Tomatoes) are among the best of Nolan's career. Audiences gave it an \"A\" CinemaScore.'Moana' sails into second spotPG-rated films followed in the wake of \"The Odyssey.\" The Walt Disney Co.'s \"Moana\" landed in a distant second place with $19 million in its third weekend. Following its disappointing $43 million launch, the live-action remake slid 56% on its second weekend. In two weeks it collected USD 178 million worldwide, a poor result for a film that cost USD 250 million to make.'Moana' was trailed by Universal's 'Minions & Monsters' and Disney's 'Toy Story 5', both of which grossed about USD 15 million.Top 10 movies by domestic box officeWith final domestic figures being released Monday, this list factors in the estimated ticket sales for Friday through Sunday at U.S. and Canadian theaters, according to Rentrak:1. \"The Odyssey,\" $124.5 million.2. \"Moana,\" $19 million.3. \"Minions & Monsters,\" $14.8 million.4. \"Toy Story 5,\" $14.8 million.5. \"Evil Dead Burn,\" $5 million.6. \"The Invite,\" $3.9 million.7. \"Young Washington,\" $3.7 million.8. \"Obsession,\" $2.5 million.9. \"Supergirl,\" $1.5 million.10. \"Disclosure Day,\" $1.5 million.Give your child the gift of confidence! Claim your exclusive TOI Masterclass spot today!"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.source","subject":"the-odyssey-becomes-christopher-nolan-s-biggest-global-debut-of-all-time-with-264-million","wire":"culture","path":"urn:newscable-bundle:5551a22519565538ae81ffc60bfa8bb790918266c0b6d534ba3199177edf0a96","title":"â€˜The Odysseyâ€™ Becomes Christopher Nolanâ€™s Biggest Global Debut of All Time With $264 Million","url":"https://variety.com/2026/film/box-office/the-odyssey-christopher-nolan-biggest-global-debut-1236815981/","domain":"variety.com","published":"2026-07-19T17:47:17.000Z","assertedAt":"2026-07-20T04:37:52.907Z","score":80,"primary":false,"matchedTerms":["odyssey","becomes","christopher","nolan","biggest","global","debut","million"],"summary":"â€œThe Odysseyâ€ is off to an epic start at the box office. Universalâ€™s action-adventure generated $264.1 million globally over the weekend, including $139.6 million internationally and $124.5 million domestically. Itâ€™s a towering debut for a movie thatâ€™s R-rated, nearly three hours in length and isnâ€™t part of a major franchise. Of course, â€œThe Odysseyâ€ isnâ€™t [&hellip;]"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.source","subject":"public-web:fb291f6cbb1c8105a32a5bf38cae2664cd47671ffea059860aa9bb04fae9d514","wire":"culture","path":"urn:public-web-source:80283c5db2fdd64b2f499c34e3335828c403bd7a4e0116e123ac8aeb702b6f06","title":"The Odyssey has officially made box office history for Christopher Nolan","url":"https://winteriscoming.net/the-odyssey-officially-made-box-office-history-christopher-nolan","domain":"winteriscoming.net","published":"2026-07-19T23:09:56.000Z","assertedAt":"2026-07-19T23:09:56.000Z","score":70,"primary":false,"matchedTerms":["odyssey","christopher","nolan","biggest","global","debut","million"],"summary":"The Odyssey has officially made box office history for Christopher Nolan The Odyssey smashed expectations with a global debut that set new opening weekend records for Christopher Nolan. By Cody Schultz | Add us as a preferred source Matt Damon (Odysseus) in Christopher Nolan's The Odyssey. | Melinda Sue Gordon/Universal Pictures Going into The Odyssey â€™s opening weekend, the epic fantasy project from director Christopher Nolan was trending to kick off its box office run on a high note. Early projections had the film grossing approximately $200 million at the worldwide box office following strong Thursday previews and advanced ticket sales, including sold-out IMAX showings across the nation. While projections can be wrong and weâ€™ve seen more than a few blockbusters underperform at the box office this year, there was never an expectation that The Odyssey would underperform. The question really was about whether the early predictions were on the conservative side or would end up being right on the nose. Well, after an amazing weekend at the box office, The Odyssey has officially surpassed predictions and helped make history for Nolan in the process. Matt Damon (Odysseus) and Zendaya (Athena) in The Odyssey. | Image: Universal The Odyssey is now Christopher Nolanâ€™s biggest opening weekend ever During its opening weekend, The Odyssey pulled in a massive $264.1 million worldwide, which makes the film the highest-grossing opening weekend in Christopher Nolanâ€™s career. Thatâ€™s right, The Odyssey is now Nolanâ€™s biggest opening weekend in his illustrious career, besting The Dark Knight Risesâ€™ opening weekend total of $249 million by over $15 million! With its $139.6 million earnings in the international market, The Odyssey has become Nolanâ€™s biggest international opening ever ahead of The Dark Knight Rises. ( The Dark Knight Rises still holds the top spot for Nolan at the domestic box office with its $160 million to The Odyssey â€™s $124 million domestic opening.) The film also helped to make history for star Matt Damon, becoming the biggest opening ever for the Oscar-winning actor. While The Odyssey might not have made history for Nolan in the U.S., the film did lead to Nolanâ€™s biggest opening weekend of all time in a whopping 45 markets. According to Deadline , The Odyssey has become Nolanâ€™s biggest opening weekend in France, Italy, Spain, Poland, the Netherlands, and Brazil. The film also showed up strong for R-rated films. While Deadpool remains the king of R-rated opening weekends at the domestic box office, The Odyssey enjoyed the fourth-best R-rated opening behind Deadpool & Wolverine ($211.4 million), Deadpool ($132.4 million), and Deadpool 2 ($125.5 million). Still, The Odyssey can boast that it was the highest R-rated opening for a non-superhero film at the domestic box office, which is another notch in the win column for the film. Itâ€™s not at all surprising that The Odyssey has performed as well as it has at the box office. Timing likely played a key role in the filmâ€™s success, as it opens at a quieter time in the summer box office schedule for adult moviegoers. While there have been some notable blockbusters to hit theaters in the last few weeks, said releases have skewed towards the family audience with the releases of Minions and Monsters and Moana. The Odyssey also dropped two weeks before Sonyâ€™s Spider-Man: Brand New Day, which sets the film up for a strong second weekend before the Tom Holland, Zendaya, and Jon Bernthal-starring film opens and shoots to the No. 1 spot. What will be interesting is to see where The Odyssey will ultimately finish its box office run when all is said and done and where it ranks among Nolan's all-time highest-grossing film list when its theatrical run ends. That's not likely to be anytime soon, though, as we imagine Universal Pictures will keep The Odyssey in theaters for an extended run! Add us as a preferred source on Google Follow Loading recommendations... Please wait while we load personalized content recommendations Home / Fantasy Movies and Shows"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.source","subject":"public-web:bd7c6f1462b3ca8f4d623b38b4e627013f9405d16a050668ba9fa10022d4c550","wire":"culture","path":"urn:public-web-source:395b87ff02968c62a94ec6ff4be2f756b5af17ddfdfddc554e29fd24f3203ee1","title":"'The Odyssey' is Christopher Nolan's biggest global box office opening","url":"https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/business/story/2026-07-19/christopher-nolan-the-odyssey-box-office","domain":"latimes.com","published":"2026-07-19T17:36:29.367Z","assertedAt":"2026-07-19T17:36:29.367Z","score":70,"primary":false,"matchedTerms":["odyssey","christopher","nolan","biggest","global","debut","million"],"summary":"It was a very warm homecoming at the box office this weekend for Christopher Nolan's \"The Odyssey,\" as the star-studded epic grossed $124.5 million in the U.S. and Canada, a welcome and massive jolt for theaters after a series of slower weeks. The Universal Pictures film's haul outperformed studio expectations of a $117-million domestic opening and set a record for the highest-grossing opening weekend for a live-action or R-rated film so far this year. \"The Odyssey\" now ranks as the third-highest domestic debut of 2026, trailing only Disney and Pixar's \"Toy Story 5\" ($159.7 million) and Universal, Illumination and Nintendo's \"The Super Mario Galaxy Movie\" ($131.7 million). The film, which stars Matt Damon as Odysseus, brought in a total of $264.1 million worldwide, according to studio estimates. That marks the biggest global opening ever for a Nolan film. \"The Odyssey\" was produced by Nolan and his wife and producing partner Emma Thomas for their company, Syncopy, and had a production budget of about $200 million to $250 million. \"It delivers on every sort of promise,\" said Jim Orr, Universal's president of domestic distribution. \"It is totally immersive. It is great emotional storytelling. It is something that truly has to be experienced on the big screen.\" The nearly three-hour epic is the first feature to be shot entirely on Imax cameras, a feat that required extensive cooperation between Nolan and the Canadian entertainment tech company, which operates out of Playa Vista. Nolan first told Imax Chief Executive Rich Gelfond in early 2024 that he was considering making an entire film with Imax cameras and laid out what he'd need for that to happen, including a quieter and lighter camera, a way to make film reloads easier and getting enough trained projectionists. \"It took a fair amount of time and investment\" to figure out those challenges, Gelfond said. But by August 2024, the Imax team put together a series of tests to show cinematographer Hoyte van Hoytema. Two months later, Nolan saw the tests and was impressed. â€œAs filmmakers and studios integrate Imax, we become an increasingly important part of the ecosystem,\" Gelfond said. \"When a film is released in Imax or shot in Imax, I think it's a signal to audiences that it's somewhat special, and the filmmaker is really leaning in in a unique way.\" Anticipation for the film has been building for at least a year, when the first Imax 70mm tickets went on sale. Pre-sales for \"The Odyssey\" shattered the previous Imax record by nearly double, the company said. Enhanced formats made up 53% of the domestic weekend's total, with both film and digital Imax revenue comprising 23.8%. Imax 70mm comprised about 4% of that total, with Imax digital making up the rest. Non-Imax 70mm film screening revenue totaled 3%, while 35mm showings made up 0.3%. Adding to the film's mystique is Nolan's reliance on old-school Hollywood practical effects, such as his use of puppetry, animatronics and robotics in scenes with the Cyclops, as well as a real Viking boat that the actors learned to sail. The massive reception for the film is a relief for theater owners, who weathered their own rough waters in the last few weeks, as Walt Disney Co.'s live-action \"Moana\" underperformed in its opening at the box office and Universal and Illumination's \"Minions & Monsters\" had a softer debut. So far this year, the summer-to-date box office is about 7% higher than the same time period last year, though it still lags pre-pandemic summer 2019 revenue by about 9%. \"Moana\" came in second at the box office this weekend with a domestic haul of $19 million. \"Minions & Monsters\" ($14.8 million), \"Toy Story 5\" ($14.8 million) and Warner Bros. Pictures' \"Evil Dead Burn\" ($5 million) rounded out the top five, according to data from Rentrak."},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.source","subject":"the-odyssey-conquers-264m-around-the-world-best-ever-for-christopher-nolan-ahead-of-dark-knight-rises-global-b-o-sunday-update","wire":"culture","path":"urn:newscable-bundle:497fcaf0e801c471ce026789e3b36d3388a77b5db3cecaba4953271389fe670f","title":"â€˜The Odysseyâ€™ Conquers $264M+ Around The World, Best Ever For Christopher Nolan Ahead Of â€˜Dark Knight Risesâ€™ â€“ Global B.O. Sunday Update","url":"https://deadline.com/2026/07/box-office-global-the-odyssey-1236996979/","domain":"deadline.com","published":"2026-07-19T15:39:00.000Z","assertedAt":"2026-07-20T04:37:52.907Z","score":50,"primary":false,"matchedTerms":["odyssey","christopher","nolan","biggest","global"],"summary":"SUNDAY AM: Odysseusâ€™ boatload of cash from his global voyage just got bigger with Universalâ€˜s Christopher Nolan epic The Odyssey raking in $264.1M worldwide, again a record start for the director ahead of Dark Knight Rises ($249M WW). The foreign start of $139.6M is also the directorâ€™s biggest international opening ever ahead of Oppenheimer and [&hellip;]"}],"claims":[{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"public-web:4a3c23d9f60612c3103fd53cac60f534cdbbf6e500e3d127f6d61bbc031815b1","sourceUrl":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/english/hollywood/box-office/th